===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To summarize a recent development to some person with decision-making power.
#: {{ux|en|The U.S. president was '''briefed''' on the military coup and its implications on African stability.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=18 May 1987
|origdate=15 May 1987
|title=Visits Shanghai
|journal=Daily Report: China
|volume=I
|issue=095
|issueurl=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=osu.32435021558234&seq=271
|publisher=w:Foreign Broadcast Information Service
|source=Beijing [[w:Xinhua News Agency|XINHUA]]
|issn=0892-015X
|oclc=7522935
|section=People's Republic of China: International Affairs
|page=G 2
|pageurl=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=osu.32435021558234&seq=289
|text=Lubbers was '''briefed''' by Shanghai Mayor Jiang Zemin on the city's economic situation, and this evening, Lubbers attended a banquet hosted by the Shanghai Municipal Governoment{{sic|Government}}.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|legal}} To write a legal argument and submit it to a [[court]].

